\alttext(Eight initial working responses take equal positive or negative magnitudes. Their first fitted link values form two group averages. A second panel shows the intercept and slope approaching minus log three and twice log three.)

>> Four counts and one intercept

For \(y=(0,1,2,5)\), the Poisson intercept score is
\(\sum_i(y_i-\mu)=0\), so \(\widehat\mu=2\),
\(\widehat\beta=\log2\), and \(\operatorname{Var}(\widehat\beta)=1/8\).
The response-scale delta-method standard error is \(2/\sqrt8=1/\sqrt2\).
The initial means are \((0.1,1.1,2.1,5.1)\), also the initial weights, and
\(z_i=\log(y_i+0.1)-0.1/(y_i+0.1)\). Therefore the first coefficient is
\(\sum_i(y_i+0.1)z_i/8.4\), directly checkable from the working table.

At the solution, the linear terms in the deviance cancel:

$$
 D=2\left[-\log2+5\log(5/2)\right].
$$
\alttext(The Poisson deviance for counts zero, one, two and five at common fitted mean two is twice minus log two plus five times log two point five.)

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/glm_four_counts.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d; d.add_column("y",std::vector<double>{0,1,2,5});
  const dm::stats::GLM m(d,"y ~ 1",{.family=dm::stats::GLMFamily::Poisson});
  const auto w=m.working_data(), trace=m.iteration_history();
  auto observations=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  observations.points(w.numeric_column("row").values(),w.numeric_column("response").values(),"count");
  observations.abline_h(2).title("Four counts; fitted mean is two").x_label("row (zero-based)").y_label("count or mean").y_limits(-.3,6.3);
  auto path=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  path.lines(trace.numeric_column("iteration").values(),trace.numeric_column("beta:(Intercept)").values(),"IRLS");
  path.abline_h(std::log(2.0)).title("Poisson intercept iterations").x_label("completed update").y_label("log mean").y_limits(.6,1.4);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(observations).add(path).size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/glm_four_counts.svg");
  std::print("Initial working state:\n\n{}\n\nFit:\n\n{}\n\nMean-response interval:\n\n{}\n",
      w.to_md(),m.model_summary().select({"n","deviance","dispersion","iterations","converged"}).to_md(),
      m.predict_frame(d,dm::stats::GLMPredictionInterval::Confidence).head(1).to_md());
}
```
