> Checking the theory

>> Repetition changes information, not the fitted probabilities

Repeat the entire eight-row binary example \(r\) times. Its log likelihood and
information multiply by \(r\), but its maximizer is unchanged. Consequently

$$
 \widehat\beta_1(r)=2\log3,\qquad
 \operatorname{SE}\{\widehat\beta_1(r)\}=\sqrt{\frac8{3r}},\qquad
 D(r)=rD(1).
$$
\alttext(Replicating all observations leaves the slope unchanged, divides its variance by the replication count and multiplies deviance by that count.)

This is an information calculation for independent replicated responses with the same
observed pattern. Copying the same flowers would not create new independent evidence.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/glm_replication.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame base; base.add_column("x",std::vector<double>{0,0,0,0,1,1,1,1});
  base.add_column("y",std::vector<double>{0,0,0,1,0,1,1,1});
  std::vector<double> repeats,n,slope,se,reference,scaled_deviance;
  for (int r : {1,2,4,8,16,32}) {
    auto d=base; for(int j=1;j<r;++j) d=d.concat_rows(base);
    const dm::stats::GLM m(d,"y ~ x",{.family=dm::stats::GLMFamily::Binomial});
    repeats.push_back(r); n.push_back(d.nrows()); slope.push_back(m.coefficients()[1]);
    se.push_back(m.standard_errors()[1]); reference.push_back(std::sqrt(8.0/(3*r)));
    scaled_deviance.push_back(m.deviance()/r);
  }
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame out; out.add_column("repeats",repeats);out.add_column("n",n);out.add_column("slope",slope);
  out.add_column("slope_SE",se);out.add_column("exact_SE",reference);out.add_column("deviance/repeats",scaled_deviance);
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(n,reference,"exact SE",dm::RGB{37,99,235}).points(n,se,"fitted SE",dm::RGB{220,38,38});
  plot.title("Information grows with independent replication").x_label("total observations").y_label("slope standard error").y_limits(0,2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");plot.size(850,490).save_svg("build/glm_replication.svg");
  std::print("{}\n",out.to_md());
}
```
